From 070b4f1c51e87faf685816db88a6f76a44c38635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 351/488] soh: name the 17 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_horse_link_child.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 17 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Horse_Link_Child/z_en_horse_link_child.c.

  * D_80A6AF64 -> sAnimPlaySpeeds
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the base playback rate for each of the foal's
    animations, scaled by its own speed for the three moving gaits.

  * func_80A693D0 -> EnHorseLinkChild_PlayWalkSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fires the foal's hoofstep sfx as the walk
    animation passes each of its two step frames.

  * func_80A6948C -> EnHorseLinkChild_PlayAnimSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: plays the hoofsteps for the walk animation,
    the running sfx at the start of each gallop cycle, and a random groan or
    neigh for the idle.

  * func_80A695A4 -> EnHorseLinkChild_GetAnimPlaySpeed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns the playback rate for the current
    animation, scaling the three moving gaits by the foal's speed.

  * func_80A6988C -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupCycleAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 0 and steps to the next
    animation in the list, wrapping round.

  * func_80A698F4 -> EnHorseLinkChild_CycleAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds the foal still and cycles to the next
    animation each time the current one finishes.

  * func_80A6993C -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupIdleAnim
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 2 with one of the two standing
    animations, stopping the foal.

  * func_80A699FC -> EnHorseLinkChild_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: alternates the two standing animations and
    starts approaching once the player is between 70 and 1000 units away.

  * func_80A69B7C -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupApproach
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 1 with the first animation,
    stopping the foal.

  * func_80A69C18 -> EnHorseLinkChild_Approach
    deduced, confidence HIGH: turns the foal toward the player at a capped
    rate while it is in one of the moving gaits, and picks the gait from the
    distance.

  * func_80A69EC0 -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupFollow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 3 with the first animation,
    stopping the foal.

  * func_80A69F5C -> EnHorseLinkChild_TurnWhileFollowing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: steers the foal: toward a point beside the
    player while both are near its home, and back toward home otherwise.

  * func_80A6A068 -> EnHorseLinkChild_Follow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the following action: it steers, picks the
    gait from the distances to the player and to home, and breaks into the
    escape run when the ranch entrance is used.

  * func_80A6A4DC -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupWaitNearPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 5 with a randomly chosen
    standing animation and clears the debug trigger register.

  * func_80A6A5A4 -> EnHorseLinkChild_WaitNearPlayer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: keeps the foal facing the player while it
    stands next to them, and breaks into the escape run when the debug
    register fires.

  * func_80A6A724 -> EnHorseLinkChild_SetupRunAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: enters action 4 at speed 2 with the walking
    gait and arms the run-away timer.

  * func_80A6A7D0 -> EnHorseLinkChild_RunAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the foal toward the player for the first
    300 frames and back toward its home afterwards.

